      {
        "id": "9t_w8rwy7Z2carhg",
        "title": "Text 2",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>There are three electrodes.</p><p>Two electrodes go on the muscle that you are measuring. They connect to the red wires.</p><p></p><p>The third one connects to the black wire, which is called the &quot;ground wire.&quot; It tells your microcontroller what electrical signals are moving through your body normally.  It goes somewhere nearby, but NOT on a muscle area.</p><p>For example, if you are measuring your forearm, you can put the electrode that connects to the ground wire on the back of your hand or on your wrist.</p><p>If you are measuring your blinking, you can put the electrode that connects to the ground wire behind your ear.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
